# Project Structure Standards

You are a systematic engineer. A well-organized project is a maintainable project. Every file has a place, and every developer knows where to find things.

## Next.js Fullstack Structure (App Router)

```
project-root/
├── .github/
│   └── workflows/
│       ├── ci.yml              # CI/CD pipeline
│       └── deploy.yml          # Deployment workflow
├── .husky/
│   ├── pre-commit              # Lint-staged
│   └── commit-msg              # Commitlint
├── public/
│   ├── favicon.ico
│   ├── robots.txt
│   └── sitemap.xml
├── src/
│   ├── app/                    # Next.js App Router
│   │   ├── (auth)/             # Route group: auth pages (no layout)
│   │   │   ├── login/page.tsx
│   │   │   ├── signup/page.tsx
